//   of every bird of the flock, of the two wheels, of the twelve before her faces and of the stacks' twelve is
//   asked against the MADE skin of every row, of the great arch's lintel and of her rock, and keeps its own reach
//   (1.12 of its size) and 1.2 m of air (BIRD_AIR): a round too near a row or the lintel is lifted by half metres
//   (30 m at the most); one too near her rock is carried out along its own outward side (a wheel that lies
//   outward draws in, 12 m at the most; any other round 3 m at the most). Her rock is asked at her list alone (her
