const GANNET = { span: [1.7, 1.9], dealt: [1.8, 2.7], top: [0.5, 0.52, 0.55], under: [0.92, 0.92, 0.9], tip: [0.07, 0.07, 0.08], sun: 0.6 /* (n3, stage L2, L2-4: 0.42 before) a bird the sun strikes is pale */, sky: 0.5, bounce: [0.1, 0.14], back: 0.03, body: [0.72, 0.72, 0.7], round: 0.35, arch: 0.3, flap: 0.4, droop: 0.25 /* (n6, stage J, J8 a) the body's own tone and its share of the sun as a round thing; the wing's arch (0.22 before), its beat (0.16 before) and its trailing edge's hang, in spans' halves */ }, birdSize = (s) => (GANNET.span[0] + (GANNET.span[1] - GANNET.span[0]) * Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (s - GANNET.dealt[0]) / (GANNET.dealt[1] - GANNET.dealt[0])))) / 1.9;      // (n3, stage L, L5) THE BIRDS AT A GANNET'S TRUE SIZE AND IN THE PLACE'S LIGHT: every bird's span is span 1.7 to 1.9 m (the one bird's form is 1.9 units from tip to tip: birdSize gives its scale from its dealt size, dealt; 1.9 to 2.7 m on the wing and 2.9 to 4.4 m on the ledges before), its body 0.87 to 0.97 m. A bird is no white light of its own: its upper side (top), its under side (under) and its dark wing ends (tip) take the sun (sun, where the bird is not in her shade), the sky by the side's own facing (sky) and the light the sea throws up under it (bounce: of the sun's where the sea under it is lit, of the sky's everywhere; back: the warm light the lit rock and haze throw back, as on her shaded stone): in her shade a bird is cool and darker than the bright sky behind it. No place and no count is changed; nothing of the lens
const SHADE_OLD = 0, HARD = { isle: 0.3, stack: 0.25, under: 0.1, weed: 0.75, head: 0.85 }, GRAIN = { edge: [0.9, 0.3], crack: 0, streak: 0.24, lam: 0.2, pit: 0.14, bump: 0.45, near: 80, mean: [0.469, 0.191] }, CRISP = { under: 0.4, lip: 0.25, dark: 0.5, light: 0.3, share: 0.7, bed: 0.5 }      /* (r21, D5 and D7) CRISP: HER FACE NEAR THE EYE HAS CRISP FORM: under most beds (CRISP.share of them) a hair of shade CRISP.under m deep and CRISP.dark dark on the bed beneath, on the others a pale lit lip CRISP.lip m high (CRISP.light), by the beds' own lines in the paint, drawn where a pixel is finer than the line; GRAIN.streak 0.24 (0.16): the wet streaks down her face plainer; the laminae's waves shorter along the coast (their noise 0.13 a metre; 0.06: stretched stripes near the eye). HARD.stack 0.25 (0.5: a stack's faces each lit by its own plane stood flat and faceted); CRISP.bed: a piece of her is rounded at each bed's head and turned under at its foot (the paint's normal; the made stone's own beds) */      /* (r21, A3) HER STONE NEAR THE EYE: HARD.isle 0.3 (0.8 in the twentieth pass: each quad of the skin lit by its own plane stood as a small flat patch); GRAIN: a bed's edge in the paint wanders edge m (ruled before); no upright crack is painted in a bed (GRAIN.crack 0: with the beds' level lines they ruled the face into blocks); the water's streaks down the face wander and are fainter (GRAIN.streak); FACET.depth 3 and FACET.flute 1.8 (6 and 0.3: upright-sided panels between the joints; now wavering flutes); BEDS.gain 1.5 (1.3) and a third, short wave in the beds' roll; LAMINAE a third of a metre thick that waver along the coast, and weathered PITS, both filtered to their mean by depth (near m); the laminae tilt the light a little (bump) */, UNDER_TONE = [0.055, 0.065, 0.065], FACET = { depth: 3, bias: 0.8, flute: 1.8, split: 0.5, own: 0.45, wander: 4, ease: 2 }, BEDS = { thick: [2, 12], gain: 1.5, least: 1, hollow: 0, hollowDeep: 2.0, roll: [110, 31, 0.5, 9.5, 0.2] }, CAVE = { great: false, small: false, east: [] /* (r21, STAGE G, G1c, the lead's order by the owner's standing term that nothing reads as somebody: THE CAVES COME OUT; three stood at stage F, at her outline's 4.1, 24.9 and 23.3: a dark hollow with a rim on a headland is the risk) */, deep: 0.5, dark: 0.96, black: 1, ease: [0.3, 1.25], tall: 1.2, wide: 0.85, block: 0, plain: 1, rag: 0.3, rock: { on: false, r: [2.8, 3.6], h: [1.3, 2.3], off: 0.24, out: 1.5 } }, CLEFT = { wander: 2.4, top: [0.35, 0.85], foot: [2, 16], depth: [0.2, 0.6], dark: 0.2, rag: 0.55, narrow: 0.95, slant: [0.07, 0.2], slantAt: 35 }, TURF = 0.6;      /* (eighteenth pass, K5 and D) NO ARRIS RUNS OVER MORE THAN TWO BEDS: FACET.own of a column's facet is its joint cell's own from foot to brink (all of it before: long upright ribs, pleats), the rest is dealt afresh for every TIER OF TWO BEDS, with its corner points shifted along the coast by up to FACET.wander m, eased over FACET.ease m at the tier's edge; a slab's step at its joint changes from tier to tier and dies out; CLEFT: a cleft wanders CLEFT.wander m sideways as it rises and ends between CLEFT.top of the cliff's height (plumb to the brink before: slits), opens only between CLEFT.foot m of her own height (from under the sea before: every rib between two clefts stood on a foot of its own), and is CLEFT.depth of its dealt depth (all of it before: even ribs); the hollows' edges ragged; CAVE.block 0: no block and no slab stands in a cave's mouth (a stair, a door); SHADE.floor: the shade under a ledge keeps this share of the sky's light (0.55 before: black slashes); TURF: turf on the ledges. */      // (seventeenth pass, L2) THE CLIFF'S FORM: FACET: between two joints the plan is a STRAIGHT FACET from one corner point to the next (each end standing depth * (a draw - bias) m out, unequal; half of them broken once more at a corner of their own), the round flutes at FACET.flute of themselves; BEDS: 2 to 12 m thick, each standing in or out BEDS.least m and more (the dealt step times BEDS.gain), and in BEDS.hollow of the blocks between two joints a bed's block is gone, BEDS.hollowDeep m deep, square-cut; CAVE: a sea cave is a cleft, CAVE.tall times as high and CAVE.wide as wide at the sea as dealt, narrowing straight to its top, its edges ragged
