// (eighteenth pass, C; the owner's word of 05:26: yes) WHAT THE WALL IS ROUND: over its lip, set back and low, DARK TREE TOPS and a few ROOF RIDGES stand within, and THIN SMOKES rise from beside the roofs and lean with the wind (east), on the
// world's clock. All of it is within the wall and rides with her; NOTHING stands on the wall, nobody is there, no tower, no mast, no flag. By place alone: each is dealt from the wall's own stations and her seed; from near under the wall the
